\small
\begin{tabular}
{cp{.5\textwidth}p{.35\textwidth}}
\hline
Layer       & Optimization Function   & Feedback Loops\\ 
\hline
\hline
Physical    & 
The AI assigns a score \( \text{Score}(x) = \sum_{i=1}^n w_i \cdot f_i(x) \) to each candidate, where \( f_i(x) \) is the value of feature \( i \) for candidate \( x \), and \( w_i \) is the weight for feature \( i \) derived from historical hiring data. Let \( C \) represent the set of all candidates. The objective is to select a subset \( X \) of size \( k \) such that: \( \max_{X \subseteq C, |X| = k} \sum_{x \in X} \text{Score}(x) \).
&  The weights $w_i$ are updated after analyzing the set of selected candidates.\\
