\section{Experiments}
\vspace{-2mm}
\subsection{Experimental Setup}
\vspace{-1mm}
We validate our method on both U-Net-based and Transformer-based diffusion models. For the U-Net architecture, we use pretrained models from the official DDPM release~\citep{ho2020denoising} available on Hugging Face. For Transformer-based models, we adopt U-ViT~\citep{bao2023all}. Our evaluations span a range of image resolutions from 32×32 to 256×256, using standard datasets including CIFAR-10~\citep{krizhevsky2009learning}, CelebA~\citep{liu2015deep}, and LSUN-Church/Bedroom~\citep{yu2015lsun}. To assess generative quality, we primarily report Fréchet Inception Distance (FID)~\citep{heusel2017gans}, where lower values indicate better visual fidelity. Without otherwise specified, all FID scores are computed using $50$k generated samples. For inference efficiency, we report the number of parameters, Multiply-Accumulate Operations (MACs), and inference speed. 
