\begin{maintheorem}
\label{thm:E}
On the lamplighter group $\Z_2 \wr \Z$, for every full shift on at least two letters, the automorphism group has a finitely-generated subgroup with co-NEXPTIME-complete word problem. For some alphabets $A$, we can use the group $\PAut(A)$.
\end{maintheorem}

