However, we need to check that the intermediate nodes on the path, i.e.\ $ha^{\ell'}$ for $\ell' < \ell$, do not branch, and that $ha^{\ell}$ does branch. This can be done since as we showed above, we have in our group automorphisms that permute $C$ in an arbitrary (even) way depending on whether a given relative node is branching. Specifically, one can use commutator formulas and divide-and-conquer to obtain a polynomial-norm automorphism that cancels the effect of $f$ if the branching is not correct.

