Let $1$ and $4$ be representatives of the equivalence classes
$\SET{1,2,3,7.1}$ and $\SET{4,5,6}$, respectively.
Then, for instance $\hat 3 = 1$ and $\hat 5 = 4$.
Furthermore, we have $\Pos_{\Val!}(s) = \SET{1,2,3,7.1,7.2}$.
