\LemmaBasicPropertiesOfXvaluedSubstitution*
\begin{proof}
Since $\CTerm{X}{s}{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$ is satisfiable, 
the constraint $\ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$ is satisfiable.
Thus, there exists a valuation $\rho$ such that 
$\vDash_{\xM,\rho} \ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$.
Take a substitution $\gamma := \rho|_{X}$.
Then, as $\FVar(\ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi}) \subseteq X$,
we have $\gamma(X \cup \FVar(\ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi})) \subseteq \Val$,
and $\vDash_\xM (\ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi})\gamma$.
Thus, $\gamma$ is $X$-valued, $\Dom(\gamma) = X$, and $\gamma \vDash_\xM \ECO{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$.
Moreover, as $\gamma(x) \in  \xV \cup \Val$ for any $x \in \xV$,  we have $\Pos(s) = \Pos(s\gamma)$.
Hence the claim follows.
