\LemInducedValidityOfRepresentativeSubstitutions*
\begin{proof}
By definition, we have that 
$Y = \SET{ w_1,\ldots,w_n }$,
$\SET{\vec{y}} = \SET{\vec{x}} \cup X$,
and
$\psi = (\varphi \land \bigwedge_{i=1}^n(s|_{p_i}=w_i))$.
Since $w_1,\ldots,w_n$ are freshly introduced variables, we have that $(X\cup\SET{\vec{x}}) \cap \SET{w_1,\ldots,w_n} = \varnothing$. % and hence $\Dom(\mu) \cap \SET{w_1,\ldots,w_n}=\varnothing$.
