The \textit{if} part follows from %%\Cref{lem:equivalence-for-renaming}.
\Cref{lem:equivalence by renaming}.
We proceed to prove the \textit{only-if} part.
Suppose $\CTerm{X}{s}{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$ and $\CTerm{Y}{t}{\vec{y}}{\psi}$ are pattern-general
and $\CTerm{X}{s}{\vec{x}}{\varphi} \sim \CTerm{Y}{t}{\vec{y}}{\psi}$.
Then, no value appears in $s$ or $t$ and hence $\Pos_{\Val}(s) = \Pos_{\Val}(t) = \varnothing$.
Thus, by \Cref{lem:basic-derived-properties-of-equivalence} all of the following statements hold:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\Pos(s) = \Pos(t)$,
    \item $\Pos_X(s) = \Pos_Y(t)$,
    \item $\Pos_{\xV\setminus X}(s) = \Pos_{\xV\setminus Y}(t)$,
    \item $\Pos_{\xF}(s) = \Pos_{\xF\setminus \Val}(s) = \Pos_{\xF \setminus \Val}(t) = \Pos_{\xF}(t)$,
    \item $s|_p = t|_p$ for any position $p\in \Pos_{\xF \setminus \Val}(s)$ ($= \Pos_{\xF}(s) = \Pos_{\xF}(t)$),
