Let $\SET{p_1,\ldots,p_n} = \Pos_{X}(s) =\Pos_{Y}(t)$,
and $s|_{p_i} = z_i$ and $t|_{p_i} = w_i$ for $1 \leqslant i \leqslant n$.
As $\CTerm{X}{s}{\vec{x}}{\varphi}$ and $\CTerm{Y}{t}{\vec{y}}{\psi}$ are pattern-general,
$z_1,\ldots,z_n$ are pairwise distinct variables, and so are $w_1,\ldots,w_n$.
