We answer these questions in three steps, shown in Figure \ref{fig:overall-flow}. In \textbf{Part 1}, we start by studying update patterns in \textit{NewsEdits}, a large corpus of article revision histories \cite{spangher2022newsedits}. Articles update for many different reasons (e.g. factual, stylistic, etc.), and it is difficult to identify these reasons. So, we introduce \textit{NewsEdits 2.0}, a taxonomy of edit-intentions for journalistic edits (Figure \ref{fig:taxonomy-edits}), to help us do this. % \textit{First, we need to identify factual edit patterns}. 
