\section{Conclusion}
In this letter, we presented an instance-specific test-time training framework for robust speech editing in real-world scenarios. By leveraging ground-truth supervision from unedited regions and auxiliary constraints in edited segments, our approach enhances prosodic and acoustic consistency. In addition, it enables precise control over speech rate through duration adaptation. Experimental results on in-the-wild benchmark datasets demonstrate that our method outperforms existing speech editing systems across both objective and subjective metrics. 

