\subsection{Frame Labels and Granularity}
\label{ssec:label}
We devise a robust frame label set, building on the Media Frames Corpus (MFC). The MFC is a foundational data set in computational framing analysis based on \citet{boydstun_tracking_2014} theoretical framework operationalizing framing through 15 topic-agnostic frame categories. The original MFC corpus~\cite{card_media_2015} consists only of news articles; however, more recently the framework was successfully applied to other types of documents, including online forum comments~\cite{hartmann_issue_2019}, suggesting suitability for our task that involves both long, formal documents and short, less formal responses.%a domain closer to the reader comments in our dataset. %For this reason, and because MFC frames were designed to be topic-agnostic, we base our label set off the MFC.
% providing span-level, headline-level, and article-level annotations. The \citet{hartmann_issue_2019} dataset consists of comments from online forum discussions annotated at the sentence level with a subset of the original MFC frame categories.

