We can further show that even $\epsilon$-approximate \emph{symmetric} equilibrium does not exist in plain presentations with two players.
\begin{restatable}{theorem}{thmeps}
  In a plain presentation, for any $F$ supported on $[V, V + 1]$ and any $c > 0$, there exists a $\Delta > 0$, such that for any positive $\eps < \Delta$, there is no pure symmetric $\epsilon$-equilibrium.
\end{restatable}
