The posteriors  corresponding to the  two  LF models (left columns  of Figure \ref{fig: bmfia_posterior_fields}) exhibit  substantial discrepancies with the HF reference posterior (right block). Their mean functions differ strongly from the HF posterior's mean function, while the uncertainty is vastly underestimated. Neither the \lfb posterior nor the \lfm posterior provides a good \emph{stand-alone} approximation of the HF posterior. Quantitatively, the posteriors are compared in Figure \ref{fig: bmfia_posterior_slices}, where we depict two diagonal slices (bottom left to top right and top left to bottom right) through the posterior field. The LF posteriors in the two bottom rows show a more than 350\% local error in their mean functions and significant bias. 

